      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Aterothrombotic disease (coronary, cerebrovascular and peripheral artery disease) is the most common cause of mortality and disability in the world, antiaggregants representing one of its therapeutic and preventive pillars. We have drugs at present that act at different levels of platelet aggregation (COX inhibitors as well as inhibitors of phosphodiesterase, ADP P2Y12 receptor and IIb/IIIa receptor). We review here the efficacy and safety of the association of antiaggregants in most relevant clinical scenarios, including current clinical recommendations and an analysis of supportive evidence."},
